{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>A talebearer.</b> Like 'your merchandise, from every merchant's powder' [Proverbs 27:16?]. The meaning is: the informer, for the merchant transfers and buys from this one and sells to that one, and the talebearer reveals to this one what he heard from that one." "<b>Do not stand upon the blood of your fellow.</b> That one not join with men of blood. And it is known how many were murdered and killed on account of informers, and Doeg the Edomite is a witness eternally." "And the meaning of <b>I am YHWH.</b> Who sees what you do in secret."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The Proverbs phrase is difficult to identify with certainty; the quotation does not match any known biblical verse exactly.", 1 "Resolved לעד ('eternally') rather than reading it as לעד ('witness'); both vocalizations are defensible."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:00.225387160Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}